    "design_review": {
      "approved_by": "design-panel",
      "at": "2026-09-21T21:00:00Z",
      "self_resolved": [
        "SPC-001 (high, verified) research.md R1 claimed MySQL 8.0.13+ supports partial unique indexes; it does not, and Django omits the constraint with models.W036 rather than failing. R1 corrected with the Django source lines, plan.md now says which mechanism carries on which backend, T024 requires the row lock to carry a comment saying it is the only thing holding FR-007 on MySQL, and D11 records what a MySQL-backed host project is promised",
        "ARC-001 (low, verified, removes work) the planned VersionQuerySet.bulk_update() override is redundant \u2014 Django's bulk_update calls .update() internally (query.py:920-923). Dropped from plan.md and T031; T030's bulk_update test stays as regression cover",
        "carried from ARC-001's evidence: bulk_update keys update_kwargs on field.attname, so the frozen-field guard compares name and attname both, or document_id slips past. Written into plan.md and T031"
      ]
    }
  },
